cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research proposal, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "BandGap-TH: Bandwidth versus Companding in Thai Audio Deepfake Detection under Telephone-Band Conditions"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "punyo_o"
repository-code: "https://github.com/punyopan/ysc"
url: "https://github.com/punyopan/ysc"
license: MIT
version: 0.5.0
date-released: 2026-08-19
abstract: >-
  A focused research proposal separating the two things a telephone codec does
  to audio — low-pass filtering and logarithmic requantization — which published
  work applies together and reports as a single degradation figure. Measures
  which half causes the loss in Thai audio-deepfake detection, sweeps the
  low-pass cutoff to locate a collapse threshold, and tests whether band-limited
  training recovers the loss.
keywords:
  - audio deepfake detection
  - Thai speech
  - bandwidth limitation
  - companding
  - G.711
  - telephone speech
  - data augmentation
  - anti-spoofing
